Top 20 AWS Services Every DevOps Engineer Must Know!
Cloud mein kaam karte ho? Then these are your essentials.
From compute to storage, networking to CI/CD — these services build the backbone of real-world cloud infrastructure.

Whether you’re learning AWS or working as a DevOps/Cloud Engineer, these services come up in daily tasks, projects, and interviews.

🧠 Top 20 AWS Services – Brief Use Cases:
	1.	EC2 – Run virtual machines (Linux/Windows) in the cloud.
	2.	S3 – Store and retrieve unlimited files, backups, and media.
	3.	RDS – Launch managed SQL databases (MySQL, PostgreSQL, etc).
	4.	Lambda – Run code without provisioning servers (event-driven).
	5.	VPC – Create secure, isolated cloud networks.
	6.	IAM – Manage access control, users, and roles securely.
	7.	CloudWatch – Monitor logs, metrics, and set auto-alerts.
	8.	ECS – Run Docker containers on AWS.
	9.	EKS – Fully managed Kubernetes clusters.
	10.	CloudFormation – Deploy complete infrastructure via code.
	11.	Route 53 – Domain registration and intelligent DNS routing.
	12.	SQS – Queue service to decouple and scale microservices.
	13.	SNS – Send notifications (email/SMS/lambda triggers).
	14.	CloudTrail – Track all API calls for auditing and security.
	15.	Elastic Load Balancer – Distribute traffic to multiple servers.
	16.	Auto Scaling – Automatically increase/decrease EC2 instances.
	17.	DynamoDB – High-performance NoSQL database (serverless).
	18.	EBS – Persistent block storage attached to EC2.
	19.	Secrets Manager – Securely store API keys, DB passwords, etc.
	20.	CodePipeline – Automate CI/CD workflows end-to-end.
